=== Code-to-code against OpenMC: see examples/fhr_ring_rpt_endf.rs ===
  That deck builds the reference materials and geometry properly and measures
  explicit TRISO, delta-tracked, at k = 1.36547 +/- 0.00229 against OpenMC's
  1.36510 +/- 0.00063 — +37 pcm (0.2 sigma). Its ring-RPT arm reads -116 pcm
  (0.5 sigma) against OpenMC's 1.36479 +/- 0.00067.
  Both are SINGLE DRAWS carrying ~230 pcm of statistics; a same-day re-run of
  the explicit case gave -466 pcm, which is 1.5 sigma of ordinary noise rather
  than a change. Pooling over seeds is gh:#196 / bn:op-awwi, and is not done.
  Source: verification_and_validation/ring_rpt/ring_rpt_vs_openmc.md

  THIS example's arms are NOT comparable to those numbers: illustrative
  materials, and a realised packing fraction of 0.2894 against a requested
  0.30. Its delta arm sits +1645 pcm from the OpenMC explicit result for those
  reasons, not because the two codes disagree. Use it for the treatment
  comparison above, which shares every one of those offsets across all arms.

